Interview Questions 🔥
Q1. What is Internal Fragmentation?

Memory wasted inside an allocated memory block because the process does not use the entire allocated space.

Q2. What is External Fragmentation?

Memory wasted in the form of scattered free holes between allocated memory blocks.

Q3. Which fragmentation occurs in Fixed Partitioning?

✅ Internal Fragmentation

Q4. Which fragmentation occurs in Dynamic Partitioning?

✅ External Fragmentation

Q5. Does Paging suffer from External Fragmentation?

❌ No

Because pages can be placed in any frame.

Q6. Can Compaction remove Internal Fragmentation?

❌ No

Compaction only helps with External Fragmentation.

🎯 10-Second Interview Answer

Internal Fragmentation occurs when allocated memory contains unused space inside the allocated block, while External Fragmentation occurs when free memory is split into small scattered holes between allocated blocks.
Fixed partitioning mainly suffers from Internal Fragmentation, whereas dynamic partitioning suffers from External Fragmentation.
